# Formatted documents — one style (Mac and Windows)

Anyone using Cursor on **this repository** (Mac or Windows) uses the **same** format. Do not use a Windows-only clipboard stack (CF_HTML / helper scripts) as a second format.

## Email, paste, “copy to clipboard”, “formatted document”

**One format:** standalone **HTML** (inline styles, like ElectraMet email share snippets).

- Calibri / Arial, 11pt, `#222`, max-width ~720–820px
- Headings and `<b>` for emphasis; tables with collapsed borders and gray header row
- **Inline `style=`** on elements (mail clients strip `<style>` blocks)
- Subject line in the chat reply
- Save as `.html` in the repo `Docs/` (or a temp file if throwaway)

**Copy (identical on Mac and Windows):** open the `.html` in the default browser → Select All → Copy → paste into Mail/Outlook. Formatting comes from the **rendered** page.

**Do not:** put HTML source in a fenced block as the thing to paste; tell them to paste tags into Mail; use RTF/EML/CF_HTML as a parallel standard; claim a cloud VM clipboard is their desktop Mail paste.

## Print / numbered SOP manuals (if this repo has them)

If the repo includes ElectraMet 900-011 / 900-012 / 900-013, generate Word with that repo’s SOP converter (960-001 layout). That is print/Word, not a second email format.

## Skip

Plain Markdown only if they **explicitly** ask for that.
